  "implementation": {
    "behavior": [
      "The Volc backend now publishes prepare and cancel operations through the shared TTS registry.",
      "A single generation-scoped request state owns cancellation and the active socket.",
      "Cancel marks the generation and calls shutdown on the active socket; the request thread remains the sole owner of TLS close/free and final state release.",
      "Cancellation is checked before later request stages, PCM callbacks, terminal callbacks, and return mapping.",
      "The next request starts only after the canceled owner releases the shared registry."
